  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM 2021 Ukraine Crisis Response Plan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">According to the 2021 Humanitarian Needs Overview (HNO) in Ukraine, over 3.4 million people in the country continue to be affected by the dual impact of the 7-year conflict and the COVID-19 pandemic. The present project aims to contribute to addressing the crucial humanitarian needs and building resilience of vulnerable conflict-affected populations residing in eastern Ukraine through the provision of lifesaving non-food items, essential water, sanitation, and hygiene, multipurpose cash, livelihood support and mental health and psychosocial support for vulnerable returnees, internally displaced persons and other conflict-affected individuals in Donetsk and Luhansk regions.</narrative>
  </description>
